{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"One observation: templates hardcode polling intervals \"every 10s\" (fleet.html:3) and \"every 2s\" (instance.html:2) that must match inventory `fleet_interval_seconds` / `selected_interval_seconds` — if the operator configures different intervals, the HTMX polling cadence diverges from the backend refresh cadence. The view doesn't carry the configured intervals to templates. Is PageView missing interval fields? InstanceView has no interval. This is a real complecting/drift issue: a one change (config interval) must touch template + backend; and configured interval is ignored by UI. Evidence: templates/fleet.html:3, templates/instance.html:2, inventory.go:30-33 defaults, model.go PageView/InstanceView lacking interval fields. That's a good finding — configurable intervals exist in inventory but the HTTP UI hardcodes 10s/2s.\n\nCheck: is this covered by existing jobs? canopy-tab-visibility-polling is about hidden tabs. canopy-critic-stale-selected-window was about freshness window. Nothing about template intervals matching inventory. Not in the tester list. Good, new finding.\n\nNow candidate findings list (max 5):\n\n1. `scanSystemdUnits` untested (discovery.go:44-105) — untested hotspot. Evidence: discovery_test.go only tests scanDevelopmentRoot (lines 9, 60, 132).\n2. Hardcoded deployment boundary `/misty-step/` (discovery.go:92) and `$HOME/Development/misty-step` (discovery.go:114) + hardcoded 5s discovery tick (app.go:114) — deployment policy complected into code, not configurable through the documented inventory surface; also scanSystemdUnits' filter is a substring check, not path-aware.\n3. HTMX poll intervals hardcoded in templates (fleet.html:3, instance.html:2) diverge from configurable fleet/selected intervals (inventory.go Inventory fields; model.go views carry no interval) — one config change requires touching distant files; configured values silently ignored by UI.\n\nMore candidates?\n\n4. `if-critic-logs-follow-unreachable` was filed and abandoned — skip.\n\n5. `App.selectInstance` in handlePage/handleFleet — fine.\n\n6. Check `handlePage`: `a.selectInstance(id)` then `a.pageView(id,...)` — but if id was provided via ?instance on \"/\" page and unknown → handled by instanceParam. fine.\n\n7. `main.go:30-43` — dup, skip.\n\n8. What about `README.md` claims \"Remote roots must be absolute. SSH destinations, executable paths, route identifiers, and command operands are validated before execution.\" — matches.\n\n9. README \"Trigger polling and Run outcomes remain separate signals.\" — view merges trigger PollError etc. fine.\n\n10. `sanitizeLogText` — job exists (if-critic-log-sanitize-untested, spec'd, not abandoned) → skip as duplicate.\n\n11. `bearerPattern` misnomer — style.\n\n12. Untested: `TestHandlerServesEmbeddedStaticFiles` — fine.\n\n13. `App.inventoryCopy`, `requestRefresh` — used? grep usage of inventoryCopy and requestRefresh. If unused → dead weight. Let me check. requestRefresh used in templates? It's a Go method; check calls. Also `NewCLICollectorWithRunner` used by tests; `if-critic-dead-collector-surface` covered CommandRunnerFunc/newCLICollector — check if inventoryCopy/requestRefresh were included in that job's note. Let me grep usage.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"One observation: templates hardcode polling intervals \\\"every 10s\\\" (fleet.html:3) and \\\"every 2s\\\" (instance.html:2) that must match inventory `fleet_interval_seconds` / `selected_interval_seconds` — if the operator configures different intervals, the HTMX polling cadence diverges from the backend refresh cadence. The view doesn't carry the configured intervals to templates. Is PageView missing interval fields? InstanceView has no interval. This is a real complecting/drift issue: a one change (config interval) must touch template + backend; and configured interval is ignored by UI. Evidence: templates/f