d.\n\nFinding: also note view.go freshness uses configured intervals while templates hardcode — inconsistent.\n\nNow check provenance info for the notes:\n- filed-by: critic (POWDER_AGENT env? use ${POWDER_AGENT:-critic}). Note earlier filed-by values look like \"forest-misty-step/canopy\". I'll use the env var if set, else \"critic\". Let me check env POWDER_AGENT.\n- deployment: instance + observed binary revision. The Canopy git revision: a1673eb1852c328d955e99c09d2b0022924e6f6a (worktree HEAD). Running build revision: unknown. Instance: identify deployment — previous critics used \"canopy worktree <id>-critic\". I'll use worktree 1788636942911613890-critic.\n\nLet me check POWDER_AGENT env and get exact line numbers for evidence:\n\n- discovery.go:44 func scanSystemdUnits; the misty-step filter at :91-93; discovery_test.go tests at :9,:60,:132 (scanDevelopmentRoot only).\n- discovery.go:114 hardcoded Development/misty-step; app.go:114 ticker 5s.\n- templates/fleet.html:3 \"every 10s\"; templates/instance.html:2 \"every 2s\"; inventory.go:30-33 (Inventory struct fields at model.go actually — Inventory struct is model.go:19-24; defaults inventory.go:17-19). Let me confirm line numbers: model.go Inventory at line ~20. Also main.go:48-52 applies defaults. And view.go freshnessWindow uses inventory intervals (app.go:119-133).\n\nAlso confirm run of tests/vet? Not required. Git state: detached HEAD in worktree — expected for canopy worktrees (previous critics worked similarly). Fine.\n\nVerify exact line numbers quickly."}}
