lse\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"canopy-critic-discovery-hardcoded-boundary\",\n  \"title\": \"Deployment-specific discovery boundary and cadence are hardcoded with no config or ADR\",\n  \"spec\": \"\",\n  \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n  \"blocked_by\": [],\n  \"lease\": null,\n  \"ask\": null,\n  \"proof\": null,\n  \"abandoned\": false,\n  \"notes\": [\n    {\n      \"at\": \"2026-09-05T19:40:51.959Z\",\n      \"by\": \"forest-misty-step/canopy\",\n      \"text\": \"filed-by: forest-misty-step/canopy @ misty-step/canopy\\ndeployment: canopy worktree 1788636942911613890-critic, git a1673eb1852c328d955e99c09d2b0022924e6f6a (running build revision unknown)\\nObserved: discovery.go:92 hardcodes the literal substring \\\"/misty-step/\\\" as the only accepted systemd WorkingDirectory (a contains() check, not path-aware), discovery.go:114 hardcodes $HOME/Development/misty-step as the sole scanned checkout parent, and app.go:114 hardcodes a 5-second discovery ticker. None of these deployment policies are configurable through the documented Inventory surface (model.go:21-26, README.md Inventory section) and no ADR under docs/adr records the choice; changing where Forests live requires editing code. Required: deployment-specific paths and cadence come from configuration (README names inventory as the configuration surface) or are recorded as accepted ADRs. Proposed spec direction: either add inventory fields for the discovery roots/boundary and cadence, or accept an ADR that pins Canopy to the Misty Step layout and document the constants in one place.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"created_by\": \"none\",\n  \"promoted_by\": null,\n  \"promoted_at\": null,\n  \"promotions\": [],\n  \"created_at\": \"2026-09-05T19:40:32.517Z\",\n  \"updated_at\": \"2026-09-05T19:40:51.959Z\",\n  \"derived\": {\n    \"terminal\": false,\n    \"waiting\": false,\n    \"open\": true,\n    \"live\": false,\n    \"takeable\": false\n  }\n}\n{\n  \"id\": \"canopy-critic-template-intervals-drift\",\n  \"title