test coverage of scanSystemdUnits and the /misty-step/ check.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_2b1b399e325c416cbb9794b9","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"grep -n \"misty-step\\|Development\" discovery.go; echo ---; grep -n \"\" main.go | sed -n '30,45p'; echo ---; grep -n \"scanSystemdUnits\\|systemctl\\|Development\\|resolveForestBinary\\|sanitizeID\\|formatLabel\" discovery_test.go; echo ---; grep -n \"handleLogs\\|follow\\|evicted\\|retained\" server_test.go | head -20"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_4868082c39b44047a2a2f4b1","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"powder list --repo misty-step/canopy 2>&1 | head -40"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":19632,"output":468,"cacheRead":20800,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":334,"totalTokens":40900,"cost":{"input":0.0014724,"output":0.000117,"cacheRead":0.000312,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0019014}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788637017889,"responseId":"gen-1788637017-uYrgPzZVvnbAVHSR0qPr","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_2b1b399e325c416cbb9794b9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"22:\tscanDevelopmentRoots(candidates)\n91:\t\t\t// Ensure it falls under Misty Step Development boundary\n92:\t\t\tif !strings.Contains(workDir, \"/misty-step/\") {\n108:func scanDevelopmentRoots(out map[string]Instance) {\n114:\tscanDevelopmentRoot(filepath.Join(homeDir, \"Development\", \"misty-step\"), out)\n117:// scanDevelopmentRoot adds one discoverable instance per directory under\n123:// checkout. It is separated from scanDevelopmentRoots so unit tests can\n125:func scanDevelopmentRoot(parent string, out map[string]Instance) {\n---\n30:\tif *configPath != \"\" {\n31:\t\tloaded, err := LoadInventory(*configPath)\n32:\t\tif err != nil {\n33:\t\t\tlog.Fatalf(\"load inventory: %v\", err)\n34:\t\t}\n35:\t\tinventory = loaded\n36:\t} else {\n37:\t\t// Try default canopy.json if it exists, otherwise start with zero config\n38:\t\tif fi, err := os.Stat(\"canopy.json\"); err == nil && !fi.IsDir() {\n39:\t\t\tif loaded, err := LoadInventory(\"canopy.json\"); err == nil {\n40:\t\t\t\tinventory = loaded\n41:\t\t\t}\n42:\t\t}\n43:\t}\n44:\n45:\tif *listenOverride != \"\" {\n---\n9:func TestScanDevelopmentRootDiscoversMockedCheckouts(t *testing.T) {\n37:\tscanDevelopmentRoot(parent, out)\n60:func TestScanDevelopmentRootDiscoversForestYAMLDeclaredCheckouts(t *testing.T) {\n107:\tscanDevelopmentRoot(parent, out)\n132:func TestScanDevelopmentRootPrefersPathForestBinary(t *testing.T) {\n159:\tscanDevelopmentRoot(parent, out)\n---\n69:\tif recorder.Code != http.StatusOK || !strings.Contains(recorder.Body.String(), \"evicted\") {\n70:\t\tt.Fatalf(\"status=%d body=%q, want evicted fragment\", recorder.Code, recorder.Body.String())\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788637033343},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_4868082c39b44047a2a2f4b1","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[\n  {\n    \"id\": \"if-fleet-observability-projection\",\n    \"title\": \"External single-pane visibility across repository Forests\",\n    \"spec\": \"Purpose: give human operators one simple, beautiful, near-real-time pane for configuration and current operations across one or more independent Iron Forest instances. The pane is an operator-owned external projection. Iron Forest remains headless and the Kernel does not serve UI.\\n\\nBoundary:\\n- Collect only supported forest.cli.v2 read surfaces through explicit local or SSH routes. Never read .forest files directly.\\n- Keep independent Kernels independent. Add no coordination authority, mutation endpoint, durable event store, implicit discovery, or shared credentials.\\n- Keep the first implementation read-only. Publication beyond the operator machine requires explicit authority.\\n- An unreachable source is UNKNOWN, never healthy or empty. Show collection time, source identity, and freshness for every instance.\\n\\nSingle-pane contract:\\n- Fleet strip: repository, host/profile identity, forest version, reachability, Kernel state, active Run count, audit result, recent failure signal, last observed time, and staleness.\\n- Selected instance: resolved primary and checks; declaration roster and relevant resolved configuration; Kernel running/running-known state; live Runs with elapsed time; each trigger's state-known, running-known, Poll result, Run error, Poll error, audit error, last Run, and interval; audit baseline/audited revision/result/violations; whole-Ledger aggregates; recent Runs and failure reasons.\\n- Keep Poll result and dispatched Run outcome as separate dimensions. Read intervals from config show and aggregates from status.ledger.\\n- Fetch Run logs on demand through forest run logs --json. A completed Ledger row whose log was evicted returns CLI exit 0 with data.complete=true and data.retained=false; render that as the expected no-retained-log state. Reserve CLI exit 4 for an unknown Run identity with neither a Ledger row nor log. Never infer log presence from Ledger row age or position.\\n- Preserve every forest.cli.v2 envelope exit/error. A failed command must produce an explicit source error, not a partial healthy view.\\n\\nSelected architecture:\\n- Build one external Go process. Use the standard library for process execution, SSH invocation, HTTP, and html/template. Vendor the HTMX browser asset; use no npm toolchain.\\n- Render server-owned HTML fragments enhanced with HTMX. Keep only ephemeral snapshots in memory.\\n- Poll selected-instance read surfaces on a bounded two-second cadence and fleet summaries less often. Use server-sent events only while a live log drawer is open; do not invent a Kernel event API.\\n- Keep all routes read-only. The pane may select instances, filter Runs, refresh, and open logs; it does not cancel Runs, reset triggers, mutate trackers, or change configuration.\\n\\nFirst proof:\\n- Run outside Kernel modules against one real local instance and one deliberately unreachable inventory entry.\\n- Render current forest.cli.v2 data without fabricated values, including unknown/error states and the observed distinction between a successful Builder Poll and a failed Builder Run.\\n- Update visible instance state within two seconds of collection; show disconnected and stale states when collection stops.\\n- Open one retained Run log, show one completed Run with data.retained=false, and show one unknown Run identity returning CLI exit 4.\\n- Exercise keyboard and pointer navigation at desktop width; prevent horizontal clipping at narrow width.\\n- Measure collector command frequency and page update behavior. Do not add durable ingestion or fleet control unless this proof names an operator question snapshots cannot answer.\\n\\nAcceptance:\\n- One external pane answers: Which instances are reachable? What is running now? What failed? Is the audited primary trustworthy? What configuration and declarations are active? How fresh is each answer?\\n- The proof has no Kernel changes beyond supported read-surface corrections, no mutation routes, no second store, no npm build, and no hidden direct-file integration.\\n- Live-scenario evidence records exact commands, timestamps, source revisions, UI results, and failure handling.\",\n    \"repo\": \"misty-step/canopy\",\n    \"blocked_by\": [\n      \"if-293\"\n    ],\n    \"lease\": null,\n    \"ask\": null,\n    \"proof\": \"Published https://github.com/misty-step/canopy/commit/ae3d2b7. go test -race ./..., go vet ./..., go build, and node --check static/htmx.min.js passed. Live browser at 127.0.0.1:8080 read 1,196 Ledger Runs from current forest.cli.v2, preserved builder poll OK versus Run ERROR, rendered local fresh plus unreachable unknown, and showed retained, known-evicted, and unknown log states. HTMX 2.0.9 selection/poll swaps, keyboard focus order, 1440px desktop, and 390px mobile with no document overflow were exercised.\",\n    \"abandoned\": false,\n    \"notes\": [\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-01T23:13:55.673Z\",\n        \"by\": \"Main\",\n        \"text\": \"Operator direction 2026-09-01: many repository Forests and high agent throughput need a human-scale account of what is happening—within one project, across projects, and across agents. This is an observability projection over independent Kernels, not a dashboard, coordinator, or second authority inside Iron Forest.\\n\\nAfter `if-293` stabilizes one instance's JSON health/read surfaces, design an external Field Station-style projection. Start with an explicit inventory plus read-only SSH/local calls to `forest version/config/declaration/status/audit/run` JSON, exact Git revisions/evidence, and tracker summaries through each repository profile's CLI. Render source identity, roster/config drift, active and failed Runs, throughput/trends, accepted/rejected work, changed product/system narrative, unresolved decisions, costs when attributable, deployment state when supplied, and UNKNOWN for unreachable sources. Separate observed/evidenced/inferred/unknown claims. Preserve Misty Step and R90 access boundaries and publish nothing without operator authority.\\n\\nFirst proof: static report, no service or new database. Measure whether snapshot collection can answer operator questions and stay current. Introduce durable event ingestion only after the report names a question snapshots cannot answer. Keep this spec-less until the target repositories, projection owner/repository, retention, and publication boundary are chosen.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-02T16:00:06.664Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"text\": \"Operator clarification 2026-09-02: Iron Forest remains primarily headless, but human operators require one simple, beautiful, near-real-time pane for configuration and current operations across one or more instances. The projection may be HTML or HTMX and may live outside Iron Forest. Preserve independent Kernels and forest.cli.v2 JSON over local/SSH collection as source truth; do not add coordination authority or a second store. Replace the blanket no-dashboard framing with a boundary: no UI server in the Kernel. First design decision is raw-HTML client rendering versus an external HTMX fragment server; prove one-instance accuracy, unknown/error states, live Runs, trigger Poll-vs-Run status, audit state, configuration, and best-effort retained logs before fleet expansion.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-02T16:10:05.765Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"text\": \"Operator selected external Go + HTMX for the first live proof on 2026-09-02. Raw HTML remains the rejected comparison direction. Keep the collector/read-surface contract identical; server-render fragments, vendor HTMX, use no npm, retain no durable projection state, and expose no mutation routes.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-02T16:14:22.741Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"text\": \"Accuracy correction from the current 1,168-row Ledger: historical aggregate agents are not limited to the configured roster and include blank and legacy/composite identities such as beaver,owl. The pane must derive Run filters and aggregate rows from returned data, not hardcode declaration names. Render blank identities as Unknown/legacy and non-roster identities as Historical/legacy while keeping the current declaration roster separate. Current observed whole-Ledger pass_rate is 0.6712328767123288; never substitute prototype metrics.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"at\": \"2026-09-02T16:41:34.699Z\",\n        \"by\": \"none\",\n        \"text\": \"Repository boundary selected by the operator: Canopy is a separate misty-step/canopy codebase. Iron Forest owns forest.cli.v2; Canopy owns explicit inventory, local/SSH collection, in-memory freshness state, Go HTTP/templates, vendored HTMX, and the read-only single pane. Integration is command/schema based, never Go imports or direct .forest reads.\"\n      },\n      {\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1788637033343},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The powder list shows the big spec job \"if-fleet-observability-projection\" — apparently completed (has proof). Let me see the rest of the list (draft jobs) — the output was truncated at 40 lines. Let me check the full list to see existing jobs, particularly any critic drafts.","thinkingSignature":"[{\"type\":\"reasoning.text\",\"text\":\"The powder list shows the big spec job \\\"if-fleet-observability-projection\\\" — apparently completed (has proof). Let me see the rest of the list (draft jobs) — the output was truncated at 40 lines. Let me check the full list to see existing jobs, particularly any critic drafts.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_38661dc968c34b5c87a0acb9","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"powder list --repo misty-step/canopy 2>&1 | python3 -c \"\nimport json,sys\njobs=json.load(sys.stdin)\nfor j in jobs:\n    print(j['id'], '| spec:', bool(j.get('spec')), '| abandoned:', j['abandoned'], '| title:', j['title'][:70])\n\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"openrouter","model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","usage":{"input":2836,"output":144,"cacheRead":40384,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":63,"totalTokens":43364,"cost":{"input":0.0002127,"output":0.000036,"cacheRead":0.0006057599999999999,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0008544599999999998}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1788637033345,"responseId":"gen-1788637033-ui5Un15NWEZVHkKIe9fB","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_38661dc968c34b5c87a0acb9","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"if-fleet-observability-projection | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: External single-pane visibility across repository Forests\ncanopy-operational-multi-repo | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Operate Canopy across real repository Forests\ncanopy-reconcile-explicit-inventory | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Preserve explicit inventory during auto-discovery reconciliation\ncanopy-decouple-discovery-tests | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Decouple discovery tests from host-specific filesystem state\ncanopy-docs-discovery-alignment | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Document zero-config discovery mechanics and precedence in README\ncanopy-expand-checkout-discovery | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Discover managed repositories with forest.yaml without requiring pre-e\ncanopy-tab-visibility-polling | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Pause background HTMX polling when browser tab is inactive\ncanopy-log-drawer-experience | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Replace inline table log expansion with an accessible slide-over drawe\nif-critic-silent-canopy-config | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Malformed default canopy.json is silently ignored at startup\nif-critic-dead-collector-surface | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Unused collector and app surface: CommandRunnerFunc, newCLICollector, \nif-critic-log-sanitize-untested | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Log redaction (sanitizeLogText) has no regression tests\nif-critic-logs-follow-unreachable | spec: False | abandoned: True | title: Logs follow-polling path is unreachable in production and untested\ncanopy-tester-log-secret-redaction | spec: False | abandoned: True | title: Retained Run log rendering and secret redaction lack regression cover\ncanopy-tester-empty-inventory-rendering | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Zero-instance empty inventory page and fragment rendering lack regress\ncanopy-tester-audit-divergence-stale | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Audit master commit divergence stale trust override lacks regression c\ncanopy-tester-initial-collection-failure | spec: True | abandoned: False | title: Initial instance collection failure unknown freshness and attempted st\ncanopy-tester-route-param-validation | spec: True | aba